  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The diagram shows electric field lines between two points, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, with a small positive charge <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> placed near the center.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Which statement correctly describes the electric force acting on charge <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">The force on <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> is zero because it is at the center of the field.</li><li data-label=\"B\">The force on <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> is towards the top of the diagram, where the field lines diverge.</li><li data-label=\"C\">The force on <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> is towards the bottom of the diagram, where the field lines converge.</li><li data-label=\"D\">The force on <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> is from left to right, in the direction of the electric field lines.</li></ol>"
  },
